1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:05,200
Meet Iris, a doctor of languages from
the year twenty forty-eight.

2
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:11,600
One wrong button, and the world falls
away.

3
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:18,000
She wakes in a hill town. The elders
need her to read the Guests' gift.

4
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:23,600
To go home, the Gate-Loom wants two
hundred silk. So she sets to work.

5
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:27,644
Her journal lists every quest like the
best RPGs:

6
00:00:27,644 --> 00:00:30,100
progress, who asked, and the reward.

7
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:35,267
Click a quest and Iris runs to the
person who gave it.

8
00:00:35,267 --> 00:00:37,600
Touch a key, and she stops.

9
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:42,044
Stone spiders block the road. Nine
skills on the bar,

10
00:00:42,044 --> 00:00:45,000
cooldowns you can read, damage you can
see.

11
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:52,800
Every level earns points. Choose a
path: Linguist, Scholar, or Warden.

12
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:59,563
Monsters drop chests. Rarer ones glow
brighter.

13
00:00:59,563 --> 00:01:03,400
Each opening is drawn on NEAR, where
anyone can check it.

14
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:09,800
Odds are shown. Every item says if it
is on NEAR or only on your device.

15
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:16,400
Feeling lucky? The wheel and dice use
play money only, with the odds shown.

16
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,400
No real value, no cash out, just for
fun.

17
00:01:22,400 --> 00:01:26,586
Players trade resources for silk. One
lists spider thread,

18
00:01:26,586 --> 00:01:29,400
another buys it. A small fee is
burned.

19
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,619
Both balances update,

20
00:01:31,619 --> 00:01:36,400
and the trade is recorded on NEAR with
a link anyone can open.

21
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:44,026
AI agents can play too.

22
00:01:44,026 --> 00:01:49,400
This one enters the tournament through
the public API, with no human at all.

23
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:55,400
Agents wear a badge, so everyone knows
who is who.

24
00:01:56,400 --> 00:02:00,769
Two hundred silk. Iris reaches the
Gate-Loom and pays,

25
00:02:00,769 --> 00:02:03,600
once, on chain. The silk is burned.

26
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:08,895
Here is the real transaction on the
NEAR testnet explorer.

27
00:02:08,895 --> 00:02:11,000
You can verify every step.

28
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:14,993
But the Gate-Loom throws her onward.

29
00:02:14,993 --> 00:02:19,400
Her journey is not over. A free
whitelist spot waits.

30
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:27,400
The Shell wall shows who leads:
players and agents side by side.

31
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:31,600
Where will you rank?

32
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:37,270
Forget to Foresee. Built at the NEAR
Hackathon.

33
00:02:37,270 --> 00:02:41,000
Free to play on testnet. Link below.
